## Context

Re-rank the section-4 figures around the new reliability screen (0506):

1. **Promote** the reliability-vs-accuracy scatter (`fig_exp1_reliability.pdf`)
   into the section-4 main text as the headline quality figure.
2. **Demote** the quality-floor heatmap (`fig_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1.pdf`,
   currently Figure 4) into the annex where scoring is discussed — it is the
   per-criterion diagnostic ("which dimension did each model fail"), i.e. methods
   support, not the headline claim.
3. **Remove** the Exp1 quality spider from the paper (Figure S1, Annex D,
   `main.md` ~L401) — the scatter inherits its exact thesis ("source is the
   universal failure mode"), so the spider is now redundant in the paper.

## Constraints / traps

- **Keep the spider CODE.** Remove only the Figure S1 block from `main.md` (and
  the paper DAG target if it has a paper-only one). Do NOT delete
  `src/aedist/plot_quality_spider_exp1.py`: (a) `plot_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1`
  imports `_model_size_rank`, `_load_rows`, `_parse_optional_float` from it, and
  (b) the French slides deck (`slides/slides.tex`) still renders spiders. This is
  a paper-content edit, not a code deletion.
- **Figure numbering** is guarded by `tests/test_manuscript_figure_numbering.py`
  (gapless 1..N). Re-number after the move and update the guard.
- Captions are derived from generated artifacts/macros, not hand-typed numbers.

## Definition of done

- [ ] Scatter inserted as the section-4 quality figure with author-set title /
      labels; caption notes the four 0-reliability dots use F1 over all runs.
- [ ] Heatmap relocated to the scoring annex with an updated caption framing it
      as the per-criterion breakdown.
- [ ] Figure S1 spider block removed from `main.md`; no dangling in-text
      reference; spider module + slides untouched.
- [ ] `test_manuscript_figure_numbering.py` updated and green; figures gapless.
- [ ] `make check` and the manuscript build pass.

## First test (write before code)

```python
def test_spider_removed_but_module_kept():
    md = Path("slides/manuscript/main.md").read_text()
    assert "fig_spider_exp1_families" not in md            # figure gone from paper
    assert Path("src/aedist/plot_quality_spider_exp1.py").exists()  # code kept

def test_reliability_in_text_heatmap_in_annex():
    md = Path("slides/manuscript/main.md").read_text()
    body, annex = md.split("## Annex", 1)
    assert "fig_exp1_reliability" in body                   # scatter in main text
    assert "fig_quality_floor_heatmap_exp1" in annex        # heatmap in annex
```

## Relevant files

- `slides/manuscript/main.md` — section 4 + Annex D (Fig S1) + scoring annex
- `tests/test_manuscript_figure_numbering.py` — gapless guard
- `experiments/render.mk` — paper figure targets
- `src/aedist/plot_quality_spider_exp1.py` — KEEP (imported + slides)

